    "reading": {
        "body": "Samsung alone holds more than a third of the 311,886 patents tracked here, with 108,705 filings, while the next fourteen entities combined account for the remainder of the top fifteen.\n\nThe gap between Samsung and IBM, the second-ranked holder, is roughly 39,000 patents. IBM's 69,760 are themselves more than double Apple's 31,730. Below that top three the numbers fall steeply: NVIDIA, the dominant supplier of AI training hardware, appears tenth with 3,477 filings, and Meta, one of the largest consumers of that hardware, sits twelfth with 2,678. Patent count does not map cleanly onto compute investment or infrastructure scale, and that divergence is worth noting. A company can build and operate enormous data centers while accumulating a relatively modest patent portfolio, and vice versa.\n\nThe series data shows the total moving from 310,516 to 311,886 across the nineteen days recorded, an increment of 1,370 filings in that window. The data covers 108 companies in total but reports counts only for fifteen. What the remaining 93 companies contribute individually, and how filings are distributed across technology subfields, jurisdictions, or time periods beyond these nineteen days, is not available here.",
